#2359; I &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only conclusion III is true<b> </b></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; III &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only conclusion II is true</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; &#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; II &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">None of the above</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2311;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2379;&#2312; &#2349;&#2368; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306;</span>"],"correct_option_id":1,"solution":"<p>I: K &gt; R: K = B &gt; N &lt; H = G &lt; F &lt; R, False</p><p>II: S &lt; T: S &ge; K = B &gt; N &lt; H = G &lt; F &lt; R &ge; T, false</p><p>III: N &lt; R: N &lt; H = G &lt; F &lt; R, True</p><p>So, only conclusion III is true.</p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In this question, there are two statements showing the relation, followed by two conclusions i and ii. Assuming that the given story is true, find out which conclusion is definitely true. </p><p>Statement:</p><p>N &gt; W &ge; O = F &gt; H &lt; S &le; L = A</p><p>Conclusion:</p><p>i) H &lt; N</p><p>ii) A &gt; F</p><p>Select one of the following options</p><p>(A) Only conclusion i is logical</p><p>(B) Only conclusion ii is logical</p><p>(C) i or ii is either logical</p><p>(D) i nor ii none of the rational</p><p>(E) i and ii are both logical</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2342;&#2367;&#2326;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2325;&#2341;&#2344; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2342;&#23