76;&#2404;</p><p>&#2325;&#2341;&#2344;:</p><p>Z &le; V = J; T &ge; L = P &ge; J; R &gt; T</p><p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2359;&#2381;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;:</p><p>i) T &ge; Z</p><p>ii) R &ge; V</p><p>iii) Z &lt; P</p></span>","options":["<span class=\"eqt\">Only i and iii</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; i &#2324;&#2352; iii</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only i and iii</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; i &#2324;&#2352; iii</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">Only i</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2325;&#2375;&#2357;&#2354; I</span>","<span class=\"eqt\">All follow</span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\">&#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2360;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;</span>"],"correct_option_id":2,"solution":"<p>Z &le; V = J; T &ge; L = P &ge; J; R &gt; T Which is Z &le; V = J &le; P = L &le; T &lt; R</p><p>Conclusion:</p><p>i) T &ge; Z; Z &le; V = J &le; P = L &le; T ----- Follow</p><p>ii) R &ge; V; V = J &le; P = L &le; T &lt; R ----- does not follow</p><p>iii) Z &lt; P; Z &le; V = J &le; P ----- does not follow</p><p>So, only i follow. </p>","marks":2,"section":null},{"question":"<span class=\"eqt\"><p>In this question, there are two statements showing the relation, followed by two conclusions i and ii. Assuming that the given story is true, find out which conclusion is definitely true. </p><p>Statement:</p><p>w &gt; k = a &ge; x = n &lt; v &le; b = h</p><p>Conclusion:</p><p>i) h &gt; x</p><p>ii) n &lt; w</p><p>Select one of the following options</p><p>(A) Only conclusion i is logical</p><p>(B) Only conclusion ii is logical</p><p>(C) i or ii is either logical</p><p>(D) i nor ii none of the rational</p><p>(E) i and ii are both logical</p></span><span class=\"hqt\" style=\"display:none\"><p>&#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358